  "id": "COMPOUND:21079 - PROTEIN:5535",
  "verbalization": "Palmarumycin CP18 appears to interact with IA-LM through a series of molecular pathways, with the drug targeting multiple proteins that ultimately converge on IA-LM as a downstream effect. The first pathway links palmarumycin CP18 to Bromodomain-containing protein 4, which is targeted by Patupilone, and in turn, Patupilone targets IA-LM. The second pathway shows palmarumycin CP18 directly targeting A704, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets IA-LM. The third pathway reveals palmarumycin CP18 targeting Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, which is a target of the same compound, and which also leads to IA-LM. These findings suggest that palmarumycin CP18 exerts its effects through multiple distinct molecular mechanisms, all of which ultimately lead to the inhibition or modulation of IA-LM. The integration of these pathways highlights the drug's potential to act through diverse pathways, possibly by modulating the activity of different enzymes or proteins that are involved in the same biological process.",
